            <ArticleTitle>Untreated idiopathic aneurysm of the pulmonary artery; long-term follow-up.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>404-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 57-year-old man with an idiopathic aneurysm of the left pulmonary artery is presented. The aneurysm was stable over many decades. No such long-term follow-up of an idiopathic pulmonary aneurysm has been described previously. After 39 years there is no evidence of heart failure or pulmonary hypertension. Because corrective surgery has a variable outcome, and prognosis is suggested to be good in the idiopathic form of pulmonary aneurysm, no surgical correction was proposed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
